Following the curve from B: it sweeps clockwise around the large outer loop (top, right side, bottom, left side). At the point where the straight line C–D crosses (near the left middle), the smooth continuation of the spiral keeps curving inward as the smaller inner arc (not turning onto the straight line). That inner arc loops over the top and ends at A. The other crossings with the line C–D are passed straight through without switching.

Thus, starting at B and staying on the same smooth curve leads to endpoint A.

\boxed{A}
